 # State machines
 
 ## What they are
-A Widget Animation State Machine (WASM_ asset) picks which animation plays from inputs: Inputs (Bool, Float, Integer, Choice, Vector 2D, Trigger, Press And Hold; built-ins Hovered, Pressed, Focused, Selected, Disabled), Layers (Override / Additive, Weight, masks), States (Plays: Single Animation / Blend 1D / Blend 2D, Playback Once / Loop / Ping Pong / Hold End Pose, Speed Input, Parameters From Inputs, On Enter / On Exit actions) and Transitions (Conditions, Blend Tween / Spring / Cut, Exit Time, priority, random).
+A Widget Animation State Machine (WASM_ asset) picks which animation plays from inputs: Inputs (Bool, Float, Integer, Choice, Vector 2D, Trigger, Press And Hold; built-ins Hovered, Pressed, Focused, Selected, Disabled, Closing; pulses tested with Fired: Clicked, Hover Entered, Hover Exited, Press Started, Released, Focus Gained, Focus Lost, Double Clicked, Right Clicked, and, while the widget has focus, Accept, Back, Gamepad Face Bottom, Gamepad Face Right, Gamepad Face Left, Gamepad Face Top, Gamepad Left Shoulder, Gamepad Right Shoulder, Gamepad Left Trigger, Gamepad Right Trigger, Gamepad D-Pad Up, Gamepad D-Pad Down, Gamepad D-Pad Left, Gamepad D-Pad Right, Gamepad Menu, Gamepad View, Gamepad Left Stick Click, Gamepad Right Stick Click), Layers (Override / Additive, Weight, masks), States (Plays: Single Animation / Blend 1D / Blend 2D, Playback Once / Loop / Ping Pong / Hold End Pose, Speed Input, Parameters From Inputs, On Enter / On Exit actions) and Transitions (Conditions, Blend Tween / Spring / Cut, Exit Time, priority, random).
 
 ## Playing one
 A Widget Animation Component's State Machines entries play machines on widgets (Target Widgets, input overrides, Start On Construct). Set inputs from Blueprint (Set State Machine Bool / Number / Trigger...) or drive them from a Flow List or a View Model.
